<title>INDIA: Indian coalminers to observe three-day strike.</title>
<headline>Indian coalminers to observe three-day strike.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nearly 750,000 coalminers in India will go on a three-day strike from July 28 to protest against the government's move to privatise the coal sector, the Press Trust of India (PTI) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>PTI quoted trade union leaders as saying that the decision to strike was taken after talks with the government failed to address their demand.</p>
<p>&quot;We therefore call upon all 750,000 workers to observe strike from July 28 to July 30,&quot; PTI quoted the unions as saying.</p>
<p>Trade unions have been demanding the withdrawal of a bill introduced in parliament seeking to denationalise the coal industry.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
